# What the exhaustive run costs: wall clock per suite, and the throughput the
# two device suites printed in the same run.
#
# Windows 11 10.0.26300, RTX 3060, warm build directories (every template had
# been built already), 2026-11-27. `date`-free: the seconds are bash $SECONDS
# around each command, so they carry the process spawn and the suite, not only
# the suite. A cold checkout additionally compiles four templates and the
# inference plug-in, which is the larger cost and depends on the toolchain.
#
# Not every row is from the same invocation. The seven suites and gates above
# `negative-controls` were timed in one pass, the one that also printed the
# throughput section below; `negative-controls` was timed in a second pass that
# started about a minute after the first had finished. So `total` is the sum of
# eight separately stopped commands, not one stopwatch around one run, and the
# roughly one minute of orchestration between the two passes is not in it.

